From eae7e2998627da479a613e7fa5496036a1f73707 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: humuhumu33 <68450279+humuhumu33@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 13:01:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] feat(crypto): put the AEAD backend behind a default-on
 encryption feature

rekindle-aead brings aws-lc-rs and aws-lc-sys. An embedder that stores
plaintext only (the default PersistentStoreConfig) has no use for them, and
aws-lc-sys needs NASM on Windows, which a clean CI runner does not have.

- kappa-core: feature encryption (default on) owns the optional dependency.
  crypto::aead_backend re-exports the rekindle types, or, with the feature
  off, a key type that cannot be constructed, so encryption fails closed when
  a store is configured with a key.
- kappa-store-redb: feature encryption forwards to kappa-core; the direct
  rekindle-aead dependency goes away.

Default builds are unchanged.
